{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/984807-vtr-during-the-dark-ages","id":984807,"title":"VtR during the dark ages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-10T04:13:38-07:00","id":984807,"title":"VtR during the dark ages","content":"We are currently running a game set during the dark ages. The chronicle is powered by the V20 dark ages game, but some of my players have suggested that we change the game engine (not the setting material) to Vampire the Requiem. There is a translation guide, so the switch [on the character level] itself wouldn't be that hard.<br /> <br /> Before anyone ask, the reason for the thoughts on changing system is due to the slow combats in the old system. I haven't tried the new one, so this might be a dead end.<br /> <br /> Assuming we do make the change. What would you recommend me to buy? Are there any books that describe the period.<br /> <br /> From what I've seen VtR vampires usually fall in torpor after a certain time, during which their stats lessen. Are their any suggestions on elders in the same vein as in VtM? The reason I ask is since they will play a major part in the current chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3307-ifrippe","name":"ifrippe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T04:43:27-07:00","id":984819,"title":"","content":"Ancient Mysteries has a small Dark Era in Middle Ages, during the Crusades. It also has some Elder Merits.<br /> <br /> If I remember correctly, in 2nd Edition the Elder stats doesn't lessen during Torpor.<br /> <br /> Finally, you may be interested in two upcoming books: Dark Eras Companion will have a Vampire/Promethean Dark Era during Black Death years. And A Thousands Years of Night will be a vampire book about Elders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T06:14:43-07:00","id":984840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/984807-vtr-during-the-dark-ages?p=984819#post984819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ancient Mysteries has a small Dark Era in Middle Ages, during the Crusades. It also has some Elder Merits.<br /> <br /> If I remember correctly, in 2nd Edition the Elder stats doesn't lessen during Torpor.<br /> <br /> Finally, you may be interested in two upcoming books: Dark Eras Companion will have a Vampire/Promethean Dark Era during Black Death years. And A Thousands Years of Night will be a vampire book about Elders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the fast reply. I will get the recommended books.<br /> <br /> Gamewise, how would the &quot;feel&quot; of the game differ. From what I've heard, vampires in the Requiem aren't as super-powered as in the Masquerade. Is that true?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3307-ifrippe","name":"ifrippe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T06:33:30-07:00","id":984851,"title":"","content":"In 2nd edition they are stronger, in my opinion. Disciplines are quite potent (some basic levels of Requiem's are 6+ dots in Masquerade)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T06:35:10-07:00","id":984853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/984807-vtr-during-the-dark-ages?p=984851#post984851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 2nd edition they are stronger, in my opinion. Disciplines are quite potent (some basic levels of Requiem's are 6+ dots in Masquerade)</div> </div> </div> </div>Are there 5+ dots disciplines in Requiem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3307-ifrippe","name":"ifrippe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T06:41:52-07:00","id":984858,"title":"","content":"There are not. Devotions tend to fill that niche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T08:10:28-07:00","id":984883,"title":"","content":"You'll want the main book for VtR 2.0e and the 1e translation guide. Generally speaking some clans will become bloodlines and some disciplines may become ancillary power sets if you want. At the moment there are no rules for disciplines at 6+ dots, but you could just port those over directly. There will be some power-curve differences however since, as Thorbes points out, the writers chose to make all disciplines more potent through Devotions (combination powers), and avoid the whole 7th-Gen == godlike because dot 6 problem.<br /> <br /> Blood Potency is the biggest difference. As you're probably aware it goes up over time or with XP (and diablorie), and down during torpor. At six+ dots it increases the max attribute and skill cap. This is a big deal since you'll use those for activating disciplines almost all the time. When BP decreases you do NOT (as of 2.0e) lose access to any skills or attributes over 5, but you cannot increase them over 5 until you build up BP to six+ again. This makes awakening elders scary, but weaker than those who can manage to stay awake. And if your BP is high enough you automatically incur significant feeding restrictions/problems. Managing that is the biggest challenge to elder/high BP play, with humanity+touchstones a close second.<br /> <br /> On humanity: there are no roads or paths, so if you're using those you'll need to work around them. Best advice I've read is to make the road a merit and apply it as one of the character's touchstones. This could get mechanically complicated and I don't have the depth of experience to advise you well, but there are others here who have experimented with this.<br /> <br /> So, what to do with Generation? Well you can just swap BP for it, but that will instantly cause the feeding problems to kick in where they otherwise might not have been an issue. You also lose the ability to model &quot;pretenders&quot; to elder blood (young, lower generation characters). You could, perhaps, work around this by giving both a Generation and a Blood Potency stat, in which both Generation and BP are set to one lower than a siring vampire has, and Generation subtracts from BP for determining feeding restrictions. Or, BP is always 1 but Generation provides an identical benefit in terms of blood pool and expenditure rate, or even max attributes if you want--and then is also decreased through torpor.<br /> <br /> Or, you could do the system switch during a period when the PCs are all in torpor, meaning they wake up at 1 BP and Generation is a social factor with no mechanical impact. <br /> <br /> I'm wrestling with all of these problems as well for a DA Britain narrative campaign (read: players too old to get together anymore), and am solving it by making them mortal again, for a while.<br /> <br /> Good luck,<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T11:42:58-07:00","id":984973,"title":"","content":"In general, the power curve is a bit flatter in Requiem, particularly in 2e. It's easier for younger vampires to become powerful than it is in Masquerade, and elders aren't as godlike. Blood Potency replaces Generation - the longer a vampire is active, the more their Blood Potency increases(roughly +1 every 50 years active), which grants similar benefits to Generaton, with increased Vitae (blood point) pools, higher Vitae/turn limits, and higher Attribute maximums, but also comes with drawbacks like increased damage from sunlight, increased Torpor duration, and more restrictive feeding requirements. At 6+, one can only feed on other vampires. Once Blood Potency would reach 11, the vampire must enter Torpor (though they can enter Torpor sooner, either voluntarily or from taking too much damage). The more time a vampire spends in Torpor, the more their Blood Potency decreases (roughly -1 every 25 years in Torpor), and they lose both the benefits and the drawbacks. Now, you could easily just drop the increasing and decreasing of Blood Potency over time and say it's a fixed value determined by Generation. Alternatively, if you want Generation to matter but to have the fluctuation of power over time that Blood Potency creates, you could have Generatiom set <i>minimum</i> Blood Potency, so that a Generation 8 vampire (for example) never drops below Blood Potency 6 no matter how long they spend in Torpor. In this case you might want to have Diablerie decrease Generation instead of or in addition to its other benefits. In either case, you'll have to give some consideration to the feeding restrictions, as having all vampires from Generation 8 and under be unable to feed on anything but other vampires without spending Willpower would obviously be a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-10-2016, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T12:05:05-07:00","id":984982,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the replies everyone. Requiem is beginning to sound like a good choice for my group.<br /> <br /> I have three more questions on this matter:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>What do I lose by switching over to VtR, compared to V20 (apart from what's already been written)?</li> <li>Will the combats become faster, compared to V20 (assume 5-10 PC/NPC in each fight)?</li> <li>Is it possible to build methuselah characters? They mustn't be demigods, but a huge sub-plot is the awakening of five ancients. Do I need a special book for that or is that the upcoming one?</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3307-ifrippe","name":"ifrippe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T12:55:08-07:00","id":985013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ifrippe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/984807-vtr-during-the-dark-ages?p=984982#post984982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do I lose by switching over to VtR, compared to V20 (apart from what's already been written)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean by lose. I mean, Requiem has 5 main Clans to Masquerade's 13, but I hesitate to call that losing 8 Clans, because Clan doesn't mean the same thing in Requiem, and I prefer the 5 archetypal expressions of vampirism over the 13 highly specific organizations. A lot of unique Disciplines from Masquerade don't exist in Requiem, but the Disciplines it does have a broader in application, and the unique Disciplines can be emulated with Devotions and Bloodline Gifts, or ported over as Disciplines. Requiem has a completely different setting and no metaplot, but since you're just planning to switch systems but not settings I don't think you lose anything there. Most of the other big differences have been covered. No Generation, no Paths/Roads, no Sects, no 6+ dot Disciplines, different power curve, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ifrippe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/984807-vtr-during-the-dark-ages?p=984982#post984982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will the combats become faster, compared to V20 (assume 5-10 PC/NPC in each fight)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Much faster, yes. Combat in Chronicles of Darkness is quick, brutal, and bloody. One good hit is often enough to end a fight (though vampires' powers obviously complicate this a bit). There are no multiple attack/action powers, and each individual action requires fewer dice rolls to resolve. In V20 you roll to hit, roll to dodge, roll for damage, and roll for soak. In VtR you make one roll (penalized by the target's Defense), and if you get any successes, it's a hit. Damage = successes + weapon modifier - the target's armor. And that's it, action resolved. Much, much more efficient. Dice rolls also have fewer variables to worry about - in V20 you can adjust number of dice, the target number to roll on the die to get a success, and target number of successes. In VtR, 8 or higher is always a success, and the target number of successes is always 1; difficulty is always expressed by adding and subtracting dice from the dice pool. This is in my experience much more efficient and makes the difficulty much easier to assess as the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ifrippe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/984807-vtr-during-the-dark-ages?p=984982#post984982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to build methuselah characters? They mustn't be demigods, but a huge sub-plot is the awakening of five ancients. Do I need a special book for that or is that the upcoming one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thousand Years of Night is an upcoming book on elders in Requiem. But, I wouldn't hold your breath for it because it could be a while before it's out. It's also more concerned with elders as conspiracies than elders as individual superpowers. It shouldn't be too hard to make super powerful ancient vampires though. Give them lots of Blood Potency, lots of high-ranked Disciplines, lots of powerful Devotions, and really high Attributes and Skills, they can easily be terrifying monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}